Feature: The battery
  Each drone has a battery. The battery counts the seconds that the drone can still fly. A light
  drone has 150 s, a standard drone 240 s and a heavy drone 300 s. A drone that flies uses 1 s
  of battery each second. A drone on the ground uses none.

  When a drone flies in a tower circle that holds enemy drones, it uses more: 0.5 s each second
  for each unit of enemy weight in the circle. A drone recharges over its own base, 10 s each
  second. It also recharges in the circle of a depot that its team holds, 3 s each second, if the
  circle is not contested. A fort and the spire do not recharge a drone.

  A drone with an empty battery is down. It is out of the game where it is, and it counts for
  no circle. It is back on the ground at its base, with a full battery, 100 s later. The enemy
  gets no points for a drone that is down.

  Expectation: A drone that flies uses one second of battery each second
    Given the batteries are on
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 100 s
    And the first Blue drone is low in the mid lane
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the battery of the first Blue drone is 90 s

  Expectation: A drone over its base recharges 10 s each second
    Given the batteries are on
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 100 s
    And the first Blue drone is over its base
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the battery of the first Blue drone is 190 s

  Expectation: An enemy drone in the same circle makes a drone use more battery
    Given the batteries are on
    And the west tower is neutral
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 100 s
    And the first Blue drone is in the west circle
    And the Red drones in the west circle are 1
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the battery of the first Blue drone is 85 s

  Expectation: A depot that the team holds recharges a drone in its circle
    Given the batteries are on
    And the west tower is held by Blue
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 100 s
    And the first Blue drone is in the west circle
    And the Red drones in the west circle are 0
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the battery of the first Blue drone is 120 s

  Expectation: A depot does not recharge a drone in a contested circle
    Overrides: A depot that the team holds recharges a drone in its circle
    The circle holds a Red drone, so the depot recharges nobody.

    Given the batteries are on
    And the west tower is held by Blue
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 100 s
    And the first Blue drone is in the west circle
    And the Red drones in the west circle are 1
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
